            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0734" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant General Alvan C.
                            Gillem, Jr., to Mr. Walter S.
                            Robertson, at Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-01">1 April 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>420. Conferred with Generalissimo this afternoon reference notification to Soviet
                    Government as to presence of field team in Manchuria re 1387. Generalissimo
                    informed me that he would not make request until assured that Communist members
                    were accompanying team. Further that upon receipt of this information he would
                    further study the question before making official request of Soviet Government.
                    You will be informed at earliest moment when his decision concerning this matter
                    is made.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
